


/*This problem shares similarity with Z1, the difference here is the constraints and that you print the sum of all sums of subarrays.

Given array a
 of length n
, print the sum of each subarray sum.

For example, Array a=[1,2,3]
 has subarrays:

a1,1=[1]
. Sum = 1
.
a1,2=[1,2]
. Sum = 3
.
a1,3=[1,2,3]
. Sum = 6
.
a2,2=[2]
. Sum = 2
.
a2,3=[2,3]
. Sum = 5
.
a3,3=[3]
. Sum = 3
.
So the answer is 1+3+6+2+5+3=20
.

Input
The first line contains a single integer n
 (1≤n≤8⋅104
) — the number of elements in the array.

The second line contains n
 integers a1,a2,…,an
 (1≤ai≤105
) — the array a
 itself.

Output
Print the sum of all sums of subarrays.*/